  "text": "The longest river in the world is the Nile River.\n\nTo simplify the equation:\n\nx/2 - 1/3 = 3x/4 + 5\n\n1. Find a common denominator for the fractions, which is 12.\n2. Multiply every term by 12 to eliminate the fractions:\n\n12 * (x/2) - 12 * (1/3) = 12 * (3x/4) + 12 * 5\n\n3. Simplify each term:\n\n6x - 4 = 9x + 60\n\n4. Move all terms involving x to one side and constants to the other side:\n\n6x - 9x = 60 + 4\n\n-3x = 64\n\n5. Solve for x:\n\nx = -64/3\n\nSo, the simplified equation is:\n\nx = -64/3"
